     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 787,
       "endIndex": 898,
       "text": "**Year 4:** $235,000 + $47,000 + $129,600 (12% RSU) = **~$411,600** *(+ whatever stacks from Refreshers 1 & 2)*"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       4,
       2
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 926,
       "endIndex": 1016,
       "text": "**Years 1 & 2:** You gain a significant jump over your current ~$526k/yr comp (+~$112k/yr)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1020,
       "endIndex": 1090,
       "text": "**Years 3 & 4 (The \"Google Cliff\"):** Your initial grant drops sharply"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       2
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1092,
       "endIndex": 1333,
       "text": "While annual refreshers (which vest over 4 years at 25%/yr) will offset part of this drop, Meta\u2019s refresher and performance multipliers tend to be more aggressive, meaning long-term compensation parity requires steady performance at Google"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
       1,
       4
      ]
     },
     {
      "segment": {
       "startIndex": 1578,
       "endIndex": 1704,
       "text": "**Zero Sign-On Bonus:** It is standard practice in Big Tech for an external L6 PM recruit from Meta to receive a sign-on bonus"
