    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** alongside a base bump to **$240,000** and maintaining the **$1.08M equity** is a top-tier outcome for an L6 PM at Google. \n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nWith Google\u2019s front-loaded vesting (33% / 33% / 22% / 12%):\n\n| Component | Year 1 | Year 2 | Year 3 | Year 4 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus (20%)** | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 |\n| **New-Hire RSUs** | $356,400 *(33%)* | $356,400 *(33%)* | $237,600 *(22%)* | $129,600 *(12%)* |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $200,000* | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| **Estimated Refreshers** | \u2014 | \u2014 | ~$50,000+ | ~$100,000+ |\n| **Total Target Comp** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** | **~$575,000+** | **~$517,000+** |\n\n*\\*Note: Sign-on bonuses this large are occasionally split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k Y1 / $100k Y2), but the total cash value over your first 24 months remains the same.*\n\n#### Comparison to Staying at Meta:\n* **Year 1 Delta:** You will make **~$844k** at Google vs. **~$526k** at Meta (a net gain of **+$318,000** in your first year).\n* **2-Year Cashflow:** You will take home **~$1.49M** over two years at Google vs. **~$1.05M** at Meta (a net gain of **+$440,000**).\n* **Unvested Equity Covered:** The $200k sign-on replaces your forfeited Meta equity dollar-for-dollar in cash upfront, *while* your Google equity vests an additional **$356k** in Year 1.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why You Shouldn't Push Further\n* **Maximized Leverage:** Recruiters rarely give a $200k sign-on bonus without reaching senior approval / compensation committee exceptions. \n* **True \"Best Offer\":** When Google matches base and throws a 6-figure sign-on to bridge unvested equity, pushing further risks appearing uncalibrated or triggering candidate fatigue.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Practical Things to Double-Check Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Payout & Clawback Terms:** Clarify whether the $200k is paid out in month 1 as a lump sum (with a standard 12-month pro-rata clawback) or split over Years 1 and 2.\n2. **Start Date / Meta Bonus Cycle:** Time your start date so you don\u2019t leave Meta right before a biannual bonus or major RSU vest date if it\u2019s only a few weeks away.\n3. **Team & Scope:** Ensure you are excited about the product area and organizational support in SF.\n\n---\n\n### How to Accept\n\nSend a note to lock it in:\n\n> *\"Thank you for working with the compensation committee to put this together. This directly addresses the unvested equity and compensation continuity I was looking for.*\n> \n> *I\u2019m thrilled to accept the offer. Please send over the formal paperwork with the updated terms ($240k base, $1.08M equity, $200k sign-on), and we can finalize the start date.\"*",
